WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:02.970
Junjou Egoist

00:04.450 --> 00:05.320
Hiro-san!

00:05.640 --> 00:09.530
Should we go to Osaka tomorrow by the sleeper coach train?

00:09.800 --> 00:11.480
Huh? Sleeper coach?

00:11.620 --> 00:12.210
Yes!

00:13.120 --> 00:15.240
I got this from a patient who is a train fan.

00:15.600 --> 00:18.610
This train is going to retire after tomorrow.

00:19.440 --> 00:22.370
Why would a railway maniac give you the tickets?

00:22.440 --> 00:27.690
Well, he was so excited about getting the tickets that he threw a massive pre-party.

00:28.450 --> 00:31.180
But he got sick because of the raw oysters he ate that night.

00:31.240 --> 00:36.210
I beg you!! Please capture the final glory of the sleeper train with this cameraaaa!!

00:37.200 --> 00:38.690
And that's how things happened.

00:39.450 --> 00:44.060
It departs at 11 PM and arrives early morning on Sunday.

00:44.530 --> 00:47.460
Then we'll return on the same day. Would you-

00:47.460 --> 00:48.650
Uh... No.

00:48.810 --> 00:52.320
Work's piled up. And it won't be completed unless I work over the weekend.

00:52.600 --> 00:53.300
But...

00:53.300 --> 00:56.880
Even if you bring things up suddenly now, I still have prior commitments.

00:57.020 --> 00:58.840
I understand that, but...

00:58.840 --> 01:00.610
I said I can't go.

01:01.740 --> 01:03.420
Um... No...

01:03.720 --> 01:07.380
<i>It's not like I don't want to travel with you, but...</i>

01:07.720 --> 01:09.720
<i>...work's really piled up...</i>

01:10.250 --> 01:11.220
<i>No, but...</i>

01:11.650 --> 01:14.890
<i>if I pull an all-nighter tonight, it might... work?</i>

01:15.090 --> 01:18.640
I understand. Sorry for suddenly asking the impossible.

01:19.490 --> 01:24.330
But I promised my patient, so I'll go tomorrow anyway.

01:24.920 --> 01:26.480
I'll return on Sunday.

01:27.180 --> 01:28.650
I'll buy some souvenirs.

01:29.020 --> 01:30.500
Will you go alone?

01:30.700 --> 01:34.020
Since it's rare to get these tickets, I'll try inviting a friend.

01:34.890 --> 01:36.020
Friend...<i></i>

01:36.250 --> 01:38.360
So then, I'm heading out first.

01:39.600 --> 01:41.100
<i>A friend!?</i>

01:41.180 --> 01:44.370
<i>It can't be that flirty senior of his, can it!?</i>

01:41.880 --> 01:43.580
Hi

01:44.620 --> 01:46.860
<i>No. I won't allow that guy!</i>

01:47.010 --> 01:52.200
<i>A-And, that aside, just the fact that he considered traveling with some other than me is itself...</i>

01:54.200 --> 01:57.580
<i>Well...</i> I'm<i> the one who said I can't go.<i></i></i>

01:57.890 --> 02:01.380
<i>He'd already promised, so it would be bad if he didn't go.</i>

02:01.960 --> 02:06.500
<i>And since there's a spare ticket, he might as well give it to someone who </i>could <i>go.</i>

02:07.860 --> 02:13.780
<i>Come to think of it, even though we've been together for so long, I've never traveled with Nowaki.</i>

02:16.160 --> 02:18.620
-Saturday-<b></b>

02:18.860 --> 02:19.810
Huh!!?

02:20.480 --> 02:22.250
Hiro-san! What's up!?

02:22.480 --> 02:24.860
What the hell's up with this photoshoot?

02:24.890 --> 02:30.210
Oh, it's the train's last run, so all the fans have gathered here.

02:30.640 --> 02:33.180
Why are <i>you</i> participating in this too!?

02:33.410 --> 02:35.980
That's because I'm here in place of my patient.

02:36.450 --> 02:38.410
Actually, Hiro-san, why...?

02:39.000 --> 02:41.940
Since you said you'd go alone after all...

02:42.090 --> 02:44.980
Oh, have you come to see me off?

02:44.980 --> 02:46.980
No!

02:46.980 --> 02:47.980
Then, why-

02:47.980 --> 02:52.440
I said, I completed my work earlier than I thought.

02:55.880 --> 02:57.340
Don't make strange noises!

02:57.810 --> 03:01.090
Even though it's one way, getting a free ticket is lucky.

03:01.440 --> 03:04.490
And I've never ridden the Shindai train before.

03:04.650 --> 03:07.000
Hiro-san! Thank you very much!!

03:07.460 --> 03:11.560
To be able to travel with you makes me really happy!!

03:12.480 --> 03:13.660
<i>Stop it.</i>

03:13.820 --> 03:21.000
Shindai Express

03:13.820 --> 03:21.000
Osaka 8 Carriages

03:13.820 --> 03:21.000
Out of Service

03:16.140 --> 03:20.690
<i>Honestly, you're carelessly making me feel happy too.</i>

03:25.900 --> 03:27.680
It's quite small, huh?

03:27.780 --> 03:29.610
Because it's a second-class sleeper.

03:30.800 --> 03:32.960
The hanger's making so much noise.

03:33.060 --> 03:37.420
Oh, for that, if you turn it upside down, it'll stop making noise.

03:37.890 --> 03:40.650
Why do <i>you</i> know something like that?

03:41.380 --> 03:44.210
My patient lectured me thoroughly on this.

03:46.700 --> 03:47.770
Hiro-san,

03:49.090 --> 03:51.280
is it okay if I come over there?

03:51.890 --> 03:53.840
And where's "there"?

03:58.880 --> 04:01.400
What will you do if someone sees us?

04:01.620 --> 04:04.850
Right. For that we have the curtains.

04:04.920 --> 04:07.560
No matter how you look at it, that's no way to use it!

04:09.480 --> 04:10.380
Hiro-san...

04:11.560 --> 04:12.660
I'm sorry.

04:13.040 --> 04:16.120
I... made you pull an all-nighter, didn't I?

04:17.160 --> 04:21.920
Not-... Not really. I just happened to finish earlier than expected.

04:22.680 --> 04:25.330
Hiro-san, I'm sorry.

04:25.640 --> 04:31.480
But, I'm really happy to be able to travel together with you.

04:32.730 --> 04:33.770
What was that!?

04:33.900 --> 04:37.130
Oh, there seem to be many curves around this part.

04:37.520 --> 04:39.530
Is-Is that so...!

04:40.690 --> 04:41.420
Hiro-san...

04:51.800 --> 04:53.660
I'm very happy.

04:56.980 --> 04:58.490
Hey, Nowak-!

05:04.200 --> 05:08.860
<i>Well, he's definitely much more exhausted than me.</i>

05:18.420 --> 05:19.800
<i>Amazing!</i>

05:20.260 --> 05:25.380
<i>I've always lived in Tokyo, so it's been so long since I saw some place this dark.</i>

05:26.460 --> 05:31.460
<i>Oh yeah, back then I used to be too scared of the dark and would sleep with the lights on.</i>

05:31.980 --> 05:34.500
<i>Certainly not now though.</i>

05:34.850 --> 05:37.130
<i>Ironically, I actually like the dark.</i>

05:38.100 --> 05:42.770
<i>Ah... darkness is like Nowaki.</i>

05:44.740 --> 05:47.560
<i>It seemed impossible, but I'm glad I came.</i>

05:48.680 --> 05:50.460
<i>Where should we go tomorrow?</i>

05:51.130 --> 05:52.730
<i>Wherever's fine.</i>

05:53.170 --> 05:57.940
<i>Together with Nowaki... if it would make Nowaki happy...</i>

05:59.380 --> 06:05.450
Farewell Ceremony~

05:59.380 --> 06:05.450
Thank you for your support

05:59.560 --> 06:02.000
Just how long are you going to keep taking them!!?

06:02.000 --> 06:05.480
Huh!? But, I promised my patient!

06:06.300 --> 06:11.680
Next day on our last stop, we ate Okonomiyaki and Takoyaki and returned home.

06:11.970 --> 06:13.980
Junjou Terrorist

06:12.820 --> 06:13.960
Wait there.

06:14.170 --> 06:15.050
Okay.

06:16.500 --> 06:21.340
<i>We had a late night dinner to celebrate Shinobu getting into University.</i>

06:21.760 --> 06:22.880
Hey, you.

06:23.050 --> 06:23.880
Yes.

06:24.050 --> 06:25.610
You're a high schooler, aren't you?

06:25.970 --> 06:27.970
What are you doing here at this late time?

06:27.970 --> 06:29.970
I was having dinner.

06:30.170 --> 06:31.800
Uh, is something wrong?

06:32.020 --> 06:34.090
Are you his guardian?

06:34.260 --> 06:35.820
Uh, oh, no.

06:35.820 --> 06:37.650
A relative then?

06:37.810 --> 06:38.690
No.

06:38.690 --> 06:40.000
Then who are you?

06:40.460 --> 06:42.610
I'm his father's subordinate.

06:42.690 --> 06:44.880
Subordinate? What kind?

06:45.170 --> 06:47.520
Do you have personal identification on you?

06:47.660 --> 06:49.580
P-Personal Identification!?

06:49.810 --> 06:52.400
<i>Uh... looks like...</i>

06:52.850 --> 06:54.720
First off, who are you!?

06:54.720 --> 06:55.900
Youth correction officers.

06:55.930 --> 06:56.700
What!?

06:56.940 --> 06:59.040
<i>...they're misunderstanding...</i>

06:59.340 --> 07:02.170
I haven't done anything that needs correction!

07:02.250 --> 07:04.330
Recently, they've been increasing.

07:04.520 --> 07:06.810
Working as escorts for male clients!

07:06.900 --> 07:08.360
Shut up!!

07:08.360 --> 07:10.860
Who I date is none of your business!!

07:13.200 --> 07:15.700
Stop sulking over every little thing.

07:16.600 --> 07:20.770
Going so far as to contact the dean of the University is a bit...

07:21.200 --> 07:24.980
More like, the dinner was so good and they just ruined it.

07:25.610 --> 07:27.570
It would have been better if I had changed my clothes.

07:27.810 --> 07:31.700
But it's not like those people meant any harm.

07:32.260 --> 07:36.220
Weeell, to outsiders, this might look like an escort deal...

07:36.760 --> 07:39.820
There's a 17 year age gap after all.

07:39.820 --> 07:44.600
What's this? Don't tell me you want to call it quits after all this time because of some age gap.

07:44.810 --> 07:48.980
Well, it will cause trouble, little master.

07:49.330 --> 07:53.000
We hold good conversations about old TV programs, don't we?

07:53.100 --> 07:57.780
I've watched them when they were airing and you watch the re-runs of the re-runs of the re-runs.

07:59.140 --> 08:02.980
<i>That's right. This age gap is much more than I thought.</i>

08:03.090 --> 08:04.960
Shinobu enters high school
Me promoted to professor
Shinobu graduates from University
Me at the age of compulsory
metabolic checkups

08:03.090 --> 08:04.960
Shinobu born
Me high school 2nd year
Shinobu enters primary school
Me graduate school student

08:05.960 --> 08:08.420
What are you mulling over by yourself!?

08:08.420 --> 08:10.570
Anyway, stop worrying over small stuff!

08:11.410 --> 08:15.140
Well, you look younger than you actually are.

08:15.420 --> 08:18.490
You're the baby-face type or the cute type.

08:18.580 --> 08:19.920
Cute...!?

08:20.900 --> 08:22.040
Who is?

08:22.610 --> 08:25.720
Ah... <i>His heart is plenty manly.</i>

08:26.640 --> 08:27.940
Call your home.

08:28.220 --> 08:30.160
I'll drop you there by car.

08:30.280 --> 08:31.480
I'm staying tonight.

08:32.050 --> 08:33.020
No.

08:33.400 --> 08:35.260
Little children should sleep at home.

08:35.680 --> 08:37.120
Don't treat me like a kid!

08:37.200 --> 08:39.080
No matter how I look, you <i>are</i> a kid.

08:42.860 --> 08:44.580
Yeah, yeah! Shut up!

08:45.720 --> 08:48.080
You sure come here every single day.

08:50.260 --> 08:52.090
W-Who might you be?

08:52.180 --> 08:55.530
Lunch. I made it with the thought of eating it with you.

08:55.850 --> 08:58.130
I-I see. Thank you for that.

08:58.520 --> 09:02.360
By the way, what could possibly be the matter with that outfit of yours?

09:02.450 --> 09:04.850
Huh!? Nothing much.

09:05.300 --> 09:10.100
I'll be a freshman starting this spring. So I thought of changing my image.

09:10.100 --> 09:12.140
Oh, is that so...

09:12.850 --> 09:17.120
I thought of coming here in a suit. But I was in a hurry, so I'm like this.

09:17.420 --> 09:18.640
Suit?

09:18.730 --> 09:20.600
And what would you do by wearing one?

09:20.740 --> 09:24.980
Because, if I wore a suit, then I'd look like a working adult to anyone-

09:26.260 --> 09:27.490
Nothing!

09:29.040 --> 09:30.640
<i>Like a working adult?</i>

09:31.280 --> 09:37.010
<i>Ah! What the? Does he want to show his mature side?</i>

09:37.700 --> 09:38.560
<i>Why?</i>

09:38.800 --> 09:41.800
<i>Uh... Could it be because of </i>that<i> the other day?</i>

09:42.050 --> 09:46.420
<i>Because I was worried about our age gap, he took that to heart,</i>

09:47.440 --> 09:50.760
<i>and even if by a little bit, wanted to close it.</i>

09:51.420 --> 09:52.780
<i>Ahh...</i>

09:52.780 --> 09:54.490
Hey, let's eat lunch.

09:54.690 --> 09:56.740
I have lots of confidence in it today.

09:56.880 --> 09:59.740
Stewed eggplant and taro boiled in soy sauce,

10:00.000 --> 10:01.080
and...

10:01.320 --> 10:02.170
Shinobu.

10:02.700 --> 10:03.490
What?

10:04.410 --> 10:06.640
Just be like your usual self.

10:07.400 --> 10:08.420
My bad.

10:09.120 --> 10:10.370
I made you insecure.

10:11.440 --> 10:19.050
No, I mean, this is a problem anyone in our situation would think about at least once.

10:19.520 --> 10:22.900
But that doesn't mean that you have to change.

10:23.440 --> 10:28.680
Thinking about it, when I'll be 117 years old, you'll be 100.

10:28.960 --> 10:31.740
We'll both be old gramps then, so that,

10:31.880 --> 10:37.280
that is, the point is, I like the usual Shinobu.

10:37.330 --> 10:37.920
Uh?

10:38.100 --> 10:39.280
Please don't worry.

10:40.440 --> 10:45.210
<i>The fact that he would try hard to close the age gap between us, just because he loves me...</i>

10:45.800 --> 10:48.540
<i>how to say this, really teases me.</i>

10:49.890 --> 10:53.420
Well, that's how it is. Let's eat, eat lunch.

10:53.650 --> 10:58.440
Awesome! You're cooking skills have really improved since last time!

10:58.700 --> 11:00.130
U-Um, Miyagi!

11:00.210 --> 11:00.820
Huh?

11:01.000 --> 11:04.490
These are all ready-to-eat from the department stores.

11:05.140 --> 11:08.020
Even if a little bit, I wanted to show you my good side.

11:10.640 --> 11:11.480
Sorry.

11:12.490 --> 11:13.640
<i>This is bad.</i>

11:14.080 --> 11:16.410
<i>I must be getting old.</i>

11:17.160 --> 11:21.010
<i>Even though he's smart, this kid doing such stupid things is...</i>

11:22.520 --> 11:25.970
<i>irresistibly lovable,</i>

11:27.000 --> 11:28.210
<i> and really cute.</i>

11:30.960 --> 11:31.860
Shinobu...

11:33.580 --> 11:35.100
...stay over tonight.

11:42.500 --> 11:43.800
Here, eat!!

11:44.530 --> 11:45.650
What's this?

11:45.730 --> 11:49.890
Burnt bread

11:45.730 --> 11:49.890
Sticky fried cabbage

11:45.730 --> 11:49.890
Rice

11:45.730 --> 11:49.890
Cabbage with
Worcestershire sauce

11:45.730 --> 11:49.890
Something resembling meat

11:45.730 --> 11:49.890
Something resembling
vegetables

11:45.740 --> 11:47.480
Breakfast, obviously.

11:47.540 --> 11:49.900
I made it with building up your stamina in mind!

11:50.260 --> 11:53.660
Stop fooling around! Don't feed such harmful looking food to people!!

11:53.660 --> 11:56.860
Hah!? <i>You're</i> the one who told me to be my usual self!!

11:57.560 --> 11:58.980
Junjou Romantica

11:58.080 --> 12:01.840
Cold! What's up with all this snow!?

12:02.780 --> 12:06.010
<i>At any rate, I'm screwed for the English test.</i>

12:06.250 --> 12:07.380
<i>What should I do?</i>

12:07.620 --> 12:11.840
<i>But, if I ask Usagi, I don't think he'd just teach me for free.</i>

12:11.960 --> 12:13.640
So much snow!

12:13.770 --> 12:14.620
Yeah!

12:14.170 --> 12:15.860
<i>Kids sure have a lot of energy.</i>

12:15.860 --> 12:17.450
Let's make a snowman.

12:16.180 --> 12:22.050
<i>Oh! Now that I think about it, back then I made snowmen with Usagi before my entrance exams.</i>

12:23.200 --> 12:27.560
<i>This is the story of when I was struggling over studying for my entrance exam.</i>

12:28.700 --> 12:31.160
<i>Nii-chan, this guy really pisses me off...</i>

12:32.850 --> 12:36.220
So, I'm asking why are you using this formula here?

12:36.540 --> 12:37.930
Well, that's because...

12:38.100 --> 12:40.550
I see. You just thought of trying to use that here, huh?

12:42.290 --> 12:48.800
<i>Nii-chan's friend, The Great Lord Usami became my tutor following a course of events since last week.</i>

12:49.540 --> 12:51.930
It's gone wrong right from this step.

12:52.300 --> 12:56.090
Have a clear idea in your head of what solution you're looking for.

12:56.090 --> 12:58.250
I know! Shut up!

12:59.120 --> 13:01.520
<i>He teaches really well.</i>

13:01.850 --> 13:06.910
For a D-grade student, you sure are full of yourself, talking as if you're a know-all.

13:07.280 --> 13:11.800
Because idiots don't know they are idiots, they will always remain idiots.

13:12.970 --> 13:17.120
Shut up!! If I take time to think, I can solve these kinds of problems too!

13:17.200 --> 13:20.970
Oh! Do you plan to spend an hour for each problem?

13:23.710 --> 13:28.090
Takahiro would have gotten into Mitsuhashi University with plenty of points to spare.

13:29.630 --> 13:31.040
Enough! I'm going home!

13:33.340 --> 13:37.710
Argh, seriously! Why are you friends with someone like him!?

13:37.710 --> 13:41.230
What happened? Did you fight with Usagi?

13:41.310 --> 13:46.430
Fight aside, why does he have such a superiority complex?

13:46.810 --> 13:48.990
<i>He immediately compares me to you.</i>

13:49.560 --> 13:50.650
You think so?

13:51.000 --> 13:53.660
True, he does have a high and mighty attitude.

13:53.820 --> 13:57.660
But he's methodical, attentive to details and always thoughtful of his friends.

13:57.660 --> 14:00.730
Even though he's living alone, he keeps his house clean.

14:01.290 --> 14:03.420
<i>Nii-chan, you're being deceived.</i>

14:03.980 --> 14:07.100
<i>I really want to reveal Usami's true nature right now.</i>

14:07.320 --> 14:10.530
<i>But if I do, I don't know what will happen to me.</i>

14:11.070 --> 14:13.250
Besides, Usagi's kind, isn't he?

14:13.320 --> 14:14.190
Really?

14:14.320 --> 14:19.410
No matter what come out of his mouth, he puts others before himself.

14:19.740 --> 14:22.030
<i>That's only because the other person is you.</i>

14:22.460 --> 14:27.380
Actually, it's a real mystery as to how you become friends with him.

14:27.760 --> 14:29.200
You're total opposites.

14:29.630 --> 14:31.940
Yeah. I'm often told that.

14:32.240 --> 14:34.290
How did it begin?

14:34.720 --> 14:36.640
Ah, thank you for the food!

14:37.090 --> 14:40.660
He always gave off a strange aura,

14:40.890 --> 14:42.990
so it was difficult to get close to him.

14:43.400 --> 14:46.600
To the girls, he was certainly a high school prince.

14:47.390 --> 14:50.180
During the end of semester tests, we're always seated according to roll nos., isn't it?

14:50.510 --> 14:54.910
Coincidentally, at that time, Usagi got the seat that I normally sat in.

14:55.980 --> 14:59.730
According to what I heard, he finished the test in 10 minutes.

14:59.730 --> 15:01.730
They say he used the remaining time to write a novel on the desk.

15:02.040 --> 15:03.840
Of course, he got 100 points on his test.

15:03.930 --> 15:05.060
<i>Wow...</i>

15:05.340 --> 15:06.110
So,

15:06.140 --> 15:10.400
Hm? Don't just use people's desks for scribbling!

15:10.970 --> 15:14.730
I read it out of curiosity. It was a really good story.

15:16.040 --> 15:18.030
I was curious about what happened next.

15:19.140 --> 15:21.740
What should I do? It's a bit difficult to strike a conversation.

15:21.570 --> 15:24.290
I liked the novel.
Will you write the sequel
(if you have time left over)?
Takahashi

15:22.520 --> 15:24.340
That's why on Usagi's desk

15:26.200 --> 15:31.680
Since then, every time there was a test, I received my personal novel series.

15:32.050 --> 15:35.570
Oh, of course, he got perfect scores across the board.

15:35.730 --> 15:36.990
Wow...

15:37.330 --> 15:39.160
When the test was over,

15:39.580 --> 15:42.640
Usami! You have amazing talent!

15:43.020 --> 15:44.620
It was very interesting!

15:46.070 --> 15:47.320
We've been friends since then.

15:47.630 --> 15:48.790
What the heck?

15:49.740 --> 15:54.520
<i>Somehow, I can totally imagine that guys face at that moment.</i>

15:55.070 --> 15:58.770
Maybe he feels a bit lost with someone 10 years his junior.

15:59.840 --> 16:02.770
But since I've left you in Usagi's care, I feel safe.

16:03.950 --> 16:07.330
<i>What's this? He totally trusts him.</i>

16:08.060 --> 16:10.840
<i>He absolutely doesn't understand that Usagi's after him.</i>

16:12.280 --> 16:14.430
<i>That Usagi, serves him right!!</i>

16:18.910 --> 16:19.540
<i>No.</i>

16:21.160 --> 16:26.030
<i>Though he's fully aware of the fact, yet he still likes him.</i>

16:27.660 --> 16:29.440
<i>He should just give up already.</i>

16:29.880 --> 16:31.200
<i>Isn't it a waste of time?</i>

16:34.280 --> 16:37.100
<i>No matter how you think about it, it's nothing but a waste.</i>

16:39.180 --> 16:41.140
<i>Not knowing at all...</i>

16:42.180 --> 16:45.650
<i>...is probably more cruel than knowing but ignoring the fact.</i>

16:47.570 --> 16:48.990
<i>Somehow, that...</i>

16:50.160 --> 16:52.410
<i>...might be much painful.</i>

16:52.760 --> 16:55.480
Ugh! Cold! Too Cold!!!

16:55.600 --> 16:57.200
What's with this sudden change of weather?

16:57.200 --> 16:58.930
And it was still warm yesterday!

16:59.160 --> 17:01.560
Sign: Notice of train closure. Trains are currently not running due to snowy weather.

16:59.550 --> 17:01.570
<i>Ah, they've stopped after all.</i>

17:02.380 --> 17:04.650
<i>Since that day, I've been skipping studies.</i>

17:04.760 --> 17:07.210
<i>It's about time I went back, but...</i>

17:07.980 --> 17:09.700
<i>It's hard to face him.</i>

17:10.840 --> 17:13.080
<i>Well, if they're (trains) suspended, nothing can be done.</i>

17:13.250 --> 17:13.920
<i>Let's go home.</i>

17:14.250 --> 17:15.610
How long do you plan on skipping?

17:16.510 --> 17:17.960
Why are you here!!?

17:18.330 --> 17:19.710
I was on my way back home from the bookstore.

17:20.030 --> 17:21.810
Let's call it quits for today.

17:22.210 --> 17:24.220
It'll be bad if I can't return home.

17:24.540 --> 17:27.580
I don't mind, but are you okay with studies?

17:28.590 --> 17:33.000
<i>No, in fact, I think they're going extremely badly...</i>

17:33.550 --> 17:34.620
My bad.

17:34.880 --> 17:36.440
I said a bit too much.

17:37.210 --> 17:39.690
I didn't mean to compare you with Takahiro.

17:40.620 --> 17:44.850
Just that, it was so surprising to see how little you could do as compared to Takahiro, that my real thoughts just came out.

17:44.850 --> 17:46.110
You're comparing after all!!!

17:46.780 --> 17:49.010
This isn't the time to quarrel over every little thing, right?

17:50.060 --> 17:51.880
We must catch up on the progress we lost.

17:53.140 --> 17:56.730
I'm sorry for not noticing my student's feelings.

17:57.060 --> 18:01.700
Uh... Oh, no! It's not such big a deal.

18:03.060 --> 18:05.170
<i>I made him apologize first.</i>

18:05.170 --> 18:07.740
Let's go. It's a bit of a walk to the carpark.

18:09.820 --> 18:11.880
Oh, there's a book store here?

18:12.320 --> 18:14.700
Huh? Weren't you returning from the book store?

18:22.760 --> 18:27.690
<i>Could it be that Usagi-san came to pick me up?</i>

18:29.120 --> 18:32.320
Besids, Usagi's kind, isn't he?

18:32.750 --> 18:33.780
<i>What's this?</i>

18:34.410 --> 18:37.520
<i>This seems as if I just didn't want to go.</i>

18:38.020 --> 18:41.640
<i>If he apologizes first, mine doesn't get proper timing...</i>

18:41.400 --> 18:42.450
A snowman!

18:43.020 --> 18:44.810
Kids sure are having fun.

18:45.300 --> 18:48.340
It never snows this much in the city.

18:48.590 --> 18:51.300
If you want to make a snowman, now's the best chance.

18:51.710 --> 18:52.970
I haven't made one.

18:53.140 --> 18:54.480
Huh!? Really!?

18:54.920 --> 18:56.740
I don't really know how to make one.

18:58.920 --> 19:00.860
Then, I'll teach you!

19:01.080 --> 19:03.230
Actually, there's a trick to it.

19:03.380 --> 19:05.150
Alright! Let's make one!

19:05.710 --> 19:06.830
That's right.

19:07.260 --> 19:10.440
If you're teaching me, I can rest assured.

19:12.320 --> 19:14.010
Hm? What was that just now?

19:14.480 --> 19:17.310
A-Alright! Let's make a snowman!!

19:23.940 --> 19:25.470
<i>That night...</i>

19:25.840 --> 19:28.190
Great. And? How's study?

19:28.410 --> 19:29.040
Ahh!!

19:29.120 --> 19:33.280
<i>Takahashi Misaki, 18 years old, just a few days before his entrance exams.</i>

19:35.460 --> 19:36.580
<i>And so, back to the present.</i>

19:37.170 --> 19:40.500
So it's like this, about English...

19:41.180 --> 19:43.610
no matter what I do, I can't understand it well...

19:43.870 --> 19:48.800
So if possible, I was thinking, could the Great Lord possibly help me...

19:49.290 --> 19:53.720
I really can't understand why you can't comprehend something so simple?

19:55.060 --> 19:56.810
Sorry for being stupid!!

19:57.060 --> 19:59.900
It's okay!! I'll give up on English!!

20:01.810 --> 20:03.090
What now!?

20:04.960 --> 20:07.970
You can do it if you try properly, so don't give up.

20:08.890 --> 20:10.240
Which parts don't you understand?

20:11.290 --> 20:12.280
Usagi-san...

20:13.070 --> 20:15.760
However, of course, I won't teach you for free.

20:16.160 --> 20:17.120
Uh, Huh!?

20:20.290 --> 20:20.960
Stop it!!!

20:20.740 --> 20:25.890
<i>"I really shouldn't have asked this guy after all", Takahashi Misaki violently regretted. </i>

20:25.950 --> 20:35.960
